cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LM-ContextProbe, please cite it as below, together with the study whose design it builds on."
title: "LM-ContextProbe: testing whether language models shift their sensitive-data judgments with patient context the way physicians do"
type: software
abstract: >-
  LM-ContextProbe is an evaluation framework for testing whether language
  models change their judgments with patient context the way physicians do.
  It defines a paired counterfactual study design (each item labelled by
  reference observers without and then with patient context), named endpoints
  with patient-clustered statistical tests, and pipelines that run the design
  on any configured model and dataset. It is not a benchmark and ships no
  study data; a synthetic example dataset is included.
authors:
